('road_953342be764469428b8b515471116dc5','user_student_anita','Full Stack Web Development with React and Node.js',5,'{\"title\":\"Mastering Full Stack Web Development with React and Node.js in 5 Days\",\"description\":\"This intensive 5-day roadmap provides a highly practical, hands-on approach to building full-stack web applications using React for the frontend and Node.js with Express.js and MongoDB for the backend. By the end, you will have a foundational understanding of both ecosystems and built a complete CRUD application.\",\"days\":[{\"day\":1,\"title\":\"Backend Foundations: Node.js & Express.js REST APIs\",\"description\":\"Set up your development environment, understand Node.js fundamentals, and build a basic RESTful API using Express.js to handle HTTP requests.\",\"topics\":[\"Node.js installation and npm basics\",\"Introduction to Express.js\",\"Setting up an Express server\",\"Defining routes (GET, POST)\",\"Request and response objects\",\"Middleware concepts\",\"JSON data handling\",\"Using Postman for API testing\"],\"tasks\":[\"Initialize a new Node.js project with npm.\",\"Create an Express.js server that listens on a specific port.\",\"Implement a GET \\/api\\/hello route that returns a \'Hello, World!\' JSON message.\",\"Implement a GET \\/api\\/items route that returns a static array of JSON objects.\",\"Implement a POST \\/api\\/items route that adds a new item to the static array (in-memory) and returns the new item.\",\"Test all endpoints using Postman or a similar API client.\"]},{\"day\":2,\"title\":\"Data Persistence: MongoDB & Mongoose Integration\",\"description\":\"Integrate a NoSQL database (MongoDB) with your Express.js backend using Mongoose, enabling persistent data storage and CRUD operations.\",\"topics\":[\"Introduction to MongoDB (NoSQL database)\",\"Setting up MongoDB Atlas (cloud database) or local MongoDB\",\"Mongoose ODM (Object Data Modeling) for Node.js\",\"Defining Mongoose Schemas and Models\",\"Connecting Express.js to MongoDB\",\"Implementing CRUD (Create, Read, Update, Delete) operations with Mongoose\",\"Error handling for database operations\"],\"tasks\":[\"Set up a free MongoDB Atlas cluster and obtain connection string.\",\"Install Mongoose and connect your Express.js application to MongoDB.\",\"Define a Mongoose Schema and Model for a simple resource (e.g., \'Task\' with title, description, completed fields).\",\"Refactor your \\/api\\/items (or \\/api\\/tasks) routes to perform actual CRUD operations using Mongoose (e.g., `Task.find()`, `Task.create()`, `Task.findByIdAndUpdate()`, `Task.findByIdAndDelete()`).\",\"Test all new database-backed endpoints thoroughly with Postman.\"]},{\"day\":3,\"title\":\"Frontend Foundations: React.js Core Concepts\",\"description\":\"Dive into React.js, learn its core principles, and build the basic structure of your frontend application using components, state, and props.\",\"topics\":[\"Introduction to React.js and SPA concepts\",\"Setting up a React project (e.g., with Vite or Create React App)\",\"JSX syntax\",\"Functional Components and Props\",\"State management with `useState` hook\",\"Event handling in React\",\"Conditional rendering and list rendering\",\"Component composition and hierarchy\"],\"tasks\":[\"Create a new React project.\",\"Develop a simple \'Header\' component and a \'Footer\' component.\",\"Create a \'TaskItem\' component that displays a task\'s title and description, accepting task data as props.\",\"Create a \'TaskList\' component that renders a static array of tasks using the \'TaskItem\' component and `map` function.\",\"Implement a simple counter component with increment\\/decrement buttons using `useState`.\"]},{\"day\":4,\"title\":\"Frontend-Backend Integration: API Consumption & Forms\",\"description\":\"Connect your React frontend to the Node.js backend, fetch data, and enable user interaction through forms to create and update resources.\",\"topics\":[\"Making HTTP requests from React (e.g., `fetch` API or Axios)\",\"Using the `useEffect` hook for data fetching on component mount\",\"Displaying dynamic data from the backend\",\"Handling form submissions in React\",\"Controlled components for form inputs\",\"Sending POST\\/PUT requests to the backend\",\"Basic error handling and loading states in React\"],\"tasks\":[\"Integrate Axios (or use `fetch`) into your React project.\",\"Modify the \'TaskList\' component to fetch tasks from your Node.js API (`GET \\/api\\/tasks`) using `useEffect` and display them.\",\"Create a \'TaskForm\' component with input fields for title and description.\",\"Implement form submission logic in \'TaskForm\' to send a POST request to your API (`POST \\/api\\/tasks`) to create a new task.\",\"Add a button to each \'TaskItem\' to send a DELETE request to your API (`DELETE \\/api\\/tasks\\/:id`) and remove the task from the UI.\",\"Implement basic loading and error states for API calls in your React components.\"]},{\"day\":5,\"title\":\"Authentication Concepts & Deployment Considerations\",\"description\":\"Explore fundamental authentication concepts, implement basic user registration and login, and understand key considerations for deploying your full-stack application.\",\"topics\":[\"Introduction to user authentication (stateless vs. stateful)\",\"JSON Web Tokens (JWT) overview\",\"Hashing passwords (e.g., bcrypt)\",\"Implementing user registration and login routes on the backend\",\"Protecting API routes with JWT middleware\",\"Environment variables for configuration (dotenv)\",\"CORS (Cross-Origin Resource Sharing)\",\"High-level deployment strategies (e.g., Heroku, Vercel, Render)\"],\"tasks\":[\"Install `bcryptjs` and `jsonwebtoken` in your backend.\",\"Create a \'User\' Mongoose model with email and password fields.\",\"Implement backend routes for user registration (`POST \\/api\\/auth\\/register`) and login (`POST \\/api\\/auth\\/login`), hashing passwords and generating JWTs.\",\"Create a simple middleware function to verify JWTs and protect a sample backend route (e.g., `GET \\/api\\/protected`).\",\"Configure CORS in your Express.js application to allow requests from your React frontend.\",\"Discuss and research deployment options for your full-stack application (e.g., deploying backend to Render\\/Heroku, frontend to Vercel\\/Netlify).\",\"Review and refactor your code, ensuring clear separation of concerns and basic error handling.\"]}],\"topic\":\"Full Stack Web Development with React and Node.js\",\"duration\":\"5 Days\"}',1793540884);
